      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mancos was founded in 1894 near where Spanish explorers first crossed the Mancos River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mancos%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew as the primary commercial trading center for eastern Montezuma County, rivaling Dolores at its founding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mancos%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Mancos River, named Rio de los Mancos meaning \"River of the Sleeve,\" flows from the La Plata Mountains through Weber Canyon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mancos%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Bauer Bank Building, built in 1905, is the oldest surviving masonry structure in the Mancos Valley and is on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mancos%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the 1950s railroad abandonment let US 160 reroute, turning Grand Avenue into the town’s main business street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mancos%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Mancos sits at 7,000 feet, offering 276 sunny days a year and 57 inches of snowfall, a balance of mountain and forest life.",
